{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/863231-interest-check-play-by-post-vampire-the-masquerade-1e-chicago-by-night","id":863231,"title":"(Interest Check/Play By Post) Vampire: The Masquerade 1e-Chicago By Night","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-10T11:04:58-07:00","id":863231,"title":"(Interest Check/Play By Post) Vampire: The Masquerade 1e-Chicago By Night","content":"I'm just going to make this short, sweet, and simple.<br /> <br /> I want to run an old-school 1e-styled game and have been wanting to run one for a long time. And I want to use the setting that started it all, the original Chicago By Night from 1991. I intend to keep all the 1e material in mind and keep all the early installment weirdness 1e had before the rest of the World of Darkness was defined.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis game will NOT use or acknowledge the metaplot or any Revised Edition material as I don't like the metaplot and it kind of goes against that 1e feel I intend to capture. The thing is, I am thinking of making this a period piece set in the 1990's, so bear that in mind when it comes to equipment and technology.<br /> <br /> Players are limited to the main seven clans (Brujah, Gangrel, Malkavian, Nosferatu, Toreador, Tremere, Ventrue) and in the spirit of First Edition, the conflict will be between elders and neonates, the young Anarchs against the Camarilla establishment. This will be a sandbox setting and would incorporate the areas of Chicago, Gary, and Milwaukee into play.<br /> <br /> The core material we will be using for reference will be as follows....<br /> <br /> Vampire: The Masquerade Corebook, First Edition (though the 2e corebook can also work)<br /> Chicago by Night, First Edition<br /> Milwaukee by Night, First Edition<br /> <br /> Now, as an ST, I may use the Player's Guide, Storyteller's Guide, The Hunters Hunted I, and the two 2e Sabbat guides as reference, but it won't come up too much. The main focus is on the above three books.<br /> <br /> So, would any VTM fans be willing to kick it old school and take a trip back to the 90's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T21:04:41-07:00","id":864094,"title":"","content":"Sounds interesting! I would love to sign up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2779-darkeye4876","name":"Darkeye4876","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:28:27-07:00","id":864489,"title":"","content":"Definitely!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}